title: ESXi execInstalledOnly Enforcement Disabled via esxcli
id: 3d1f6c2a-9b47-4e18-8a5c-71c0a4de2f6b
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects an ESXi host where the VMkernel advanced setting
    /UserVars/ExecInstalledOnly is switched off through esxcli. The control
    blocks execution of unsigned binaries from the filesystem, so disabling it
    is the enabling step for running a dropped or uploaded ELF payload on the
    hypervisor. Kaspersky GERT documented BlackNevas ransomware doing exactly
    this in an October 2025 intrusion: after reusing a shared root password to
    log in over SSH, the operator uploaded an "esx" binary, set
    ExecInstalledOnly to 0, and cleared the logs before wiping four ESXi hosts,
    every guest VM, both vCenter Server Appliances and the backups. No
    hypervisor vulnerability was used, so configuration-plane monitoring is the
    only place this stage is visible.
references:
    - https://osintsights.com/ransomware-targets-hypervisor-layer-via-legitimate-vmware-interfaces
    - https://cyber.netsecops.io/articles/blacknevas-ransomware-wipes-vmware-environment-with-stolen-credentials/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/15
tags:
    - attack.t1675
    - attack.t1562
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: linux
detection:
    selection_setting:
        CommandLine|contains|all:
            - 'execInstalledOnly'
            - 'system settings advanced'
    selection_value:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - '-i 0'
            - '--int-value 0'
    filter_list:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'advanced list'
            - 'advanced get'
    condition: selection_setting and selection_value and not filter_list
falsepositives:
    - Administrators or backup/upgrade tooling temporarily allowing unsigned VIBs or drivers on lab and build hosts
    - Hypervisor hardening scripts that report or reset the setting during a maintenance window
level: high
